  "narrative": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The Music of Language",
        "body": "Mildred Howard's three-dimensional text runs across the Mason Street front — phrases including “Harmony and Kindness” and “Justice Like Water falls”. The city's inventory lists the work as untitled. Howard was born in San Francisco in 1945 and has held a Guggenheim Fellowship and two Rockefeller Bellagio fellowships.\nThe building was developed as a joint venture of the GLIDE Economic Development Corporation and the Tenderloin Neighborhood Development Corporation."
      }
    ]
  },
